1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:27,900
When everyone else is trying to sleep at night,

3
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:29,820
how can you be listening to music?

4
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,710
Monica, that's not true!

5
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:32,220
As a woman,

6
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,620
your figure is the most important thing of all.

7
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:36,060
But last time you said

8
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,980
that artistic temperament was the most important.

9
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:39,900
"Baby's Cradle"

10
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,740
They say you and Monica don't
look like Mother and Daughter.

11
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,180
They say you look more like her older Sister.

12
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:47,580
What really makes me mad is you
playing dumb and acting all gentle.

13
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,020
Acting weak, acting pitiful,

14
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:50,940
just to get sympathy from boys.

15
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,340
But that's just a difference in our personalities!

16
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,500
Episode 9

17
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,980
You lost one little Match and now you're all upset?

18
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,860
No, I'm not.

19
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,220
Mickey told me all about it.

20
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:35,580
A match like that isn't worth getting worked up over.

21
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:40,380
I know my Yo-Yo skills aren't that great.

22
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:42,300
But...

23
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:45,180
it feels like I just can't break through to the next level.

24
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,500
Don't be so impatient. Just take it one step at a time.

25
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:53,820
So... can you help me get better?

26
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,620
I can only offer you some advice.

27
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,540
But everyone has their own unique strengths.

28
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,430
You have to rely on your own unique traits and intuition,

29
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:04,380
and slowly figure it out for yourself.

30
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,300
Find your own feel for the Yo-Yo.

31
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:08,700
That's the only way to improve your control.

32
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:16,380
Don't be in such a rush. Haste makes waste.

33
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,660
You're always off by yourself, away from everyone else.

34
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:24,540
Is it to find your feel for the Yo-Yo?

35
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,420
Something like that.

36
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,340
But...

37
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,260
everyone says you're really weird.

38
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:34,140
And they've never seen you battle for real.

39
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:39,900
That you're just a second Shawn.

40
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,460
Did you grow up in America?

41
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:53,900
Yes.

42
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:57,180
When I was really young,
my parents and I moved to the US.

43
00:03:57,720 --> 00:04:00,540
Then why are you back here for School now?

44
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
That's...

45
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:05,340
Ah!

46
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:11,550
Why'd you scream like that? You scared me!

47
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,990
You're the one who popped out of nowhere and scared me!

48
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:14,940
I was crouching in the bushes.

49
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:17,820
Everything was so perfectly balanced and harmonious.

50
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:19,740
But then you started walking over here

51
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:22,590
and completely shattered my peaceful little World.

52
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:24,030
What do you mean, "your World"?

53
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,020
Does this path belong to you?

54
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:26,800
Do those trees and those green leaves belong to you?

55
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:28,860
Of course!

56
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:31,510
Nature is only there for those who know how to appreciate it.

57
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,180
With a loud voice like yours,

58
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:35,100
you only bring nightmares to nature.

59
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,510
You lurking around all the time

60
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:37,980
is the real nightmare for our Jianghai Team.

61
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,700
I get harassed by annoying people
like that every single day.

62
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:15,500
1, 2, 3, 4!

63
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:20,700
Go, Jianghai Team!

64
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:23,500
1, 2, 3, 4!

65
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:25,500
Go, Jianghai Team!

66
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:45,660
You little punk. Caught you red-handed.

67
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:49,500
So it was you, kid, wearing his uniform!

68
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:51,420
No, no, no, this is all a misunderstanding!

69
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,340
What misunderstanding? Let's go!

70
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:08,220
Matthew, can't you usually do

71
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:09,970
30 "Lightning Fast" in a row?

72
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:14,940
Matthew...

73
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:16,860
Is it because Monica isn't here

74
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:18,300
That's why you're messing up.

75
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:20,700
Honestly, it's better if Monica doesn't come.

76
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,070
I just can't stand her mom.

77
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,780
How come Chuck isn't back yet?

78
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:26,940
Chuck?

79
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:28,830
Chuck asked me for a bathroom break a while ago.

80
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:31,590
It's been so long. Why isn't he back yet?

81
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:35,100
Look, you guys! It's Chuck!

82
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,860
Stealing chicken and fish is bad enough,

83
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:43,260
but messing with our work and daily lives is way worse.

84
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,140
Ever since that last food theft incident,

85
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:49,020
the whole place has been on edge and in total chaos.

86
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:52,860
Yeah! Now every time we serve chicken or fish,

87
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:55,740
we have to give it a full-body inspection first,

88
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,140
just to make sure all the pieces

89
00:06:58,300 --> 00:06:59,500
are still intact.

90
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,460
And I keep having these nightmares.

91
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,790
I'll bring out a perfectly good chicken,

92
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:06,930
and suddenly a drumstick is just gone.

93
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:10,140
I mean, I love chicken legs,
but I've never laid a finger on them!

94
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:13,020
How could someone just eat it like that?

95
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:14,460
And what's worse is,

96
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,820
this kid was even wearing my uniform when he stole it!

97
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,700
If someone saw him as he got away,

98
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:24,060
they'd pin the whole thing on me!

99
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,940
This is unbearable! I won't stand for it!

100
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,500
Right. I'm ordering you right now:

101
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:32,700
Stop the Training Camp and get out of the Falcon Camp!

102
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,620
This is to ensure the safety of our kitchen!

103
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,900
Come on, let's go report this to Manager Ma!

104
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:43,260
You guys go pack your bags.

105
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:54,780
What's the point of crying now?

106
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:57,180
Yeah, Chuck. How could you do this?

107
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:59,580
Chuck, stop crying.

108
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:05,380
Your whole life, you have to fight against your own desires.

109
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:08,940
Someone who can't even overcome a simple craving for food...

110
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:14,800
Ah, desires. This is all caused by desire.

111
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:15,980
Enough!

112
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,300
Everyone else, get back to training.

113
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,940
Chuck, go back to your room and write a self-reflection.

114
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,620
We'll deal with all of this once Coach Tony gets back.

115
00:08:38,970 --> 00:08:39,420
Coach Tony.

116
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,740
Man, we've been waiting forever for you to get back.

117
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,100
What's wrong?

118
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:52,350
What's wrong?

119
00:08:53,020 --> 00:08:53,820
What's going on?

120
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:58,140
Manager Ma, I'm really sorry.

121
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,060
I know.

122
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:02,460
You're here to collect the fees for the lodging,

123
00:09:02,620 --> 00:09:04,380
and for using the Training Grounds.

124
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:09,660
But we can't let our Students find
out about something like this.

125
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,550
You didn't tell them, did you?

126
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:12,510
No, no.

127
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,980
I just asked them if you were back yet.

128
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:19,260
Well, what about the deposit?

129
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:23,100
About that, Manager Ma...

130
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,980
I've tried every possible avenue already.

131
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,900
But you know how things are right now.

132
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:31,740
We keep running into all sorts of problems.

133
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Coach Tony.

134
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:36,540
Whatever problems you have, that's not my concern.

135
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,420
I'm only responsible for collecting
the standard fees from you.

136
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:41,820
Otherwise, I can't answer to the Base Management.

137
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:42,780
Don't you agree?

138
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,000
You already know,

139
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,660
you guys have been here for over a week already.

140
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:47,580
That money's long gone.

141
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:51,900
According to the rules,
the deposit needs to be paid in advance.

142
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:53,340
Yes, yes, yes.

143
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:56,220
Manager Ma, I'm really sorry.

144
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:57,410
Could you just give us a couple more days?

145
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,550
Okay? Just a couple of days.

146
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:01,500
By the way, that chubby kid on your Team

147
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:03,900
He snuck into our kitchen again to steal food.

148
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:05,450
We caught him red-handed this time.

149
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:09,180
It's Chuck again.

150
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:12,990
Last time, we didn't manage to catch him.

151
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,430
so we had no way

152
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,860
to properly discipline him.

153
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:19,710
But this time, don't you worry,

154
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:22,140
I'll make sure he's severely punished, okay?

155
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:26,940
Some of our Staff are really upset.

156
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:30,270
They're demanding that your Jianghai Team

157
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,500
leave our Falcon Base as soon as possible.

158
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,710
Manager Ma, please, you can't do that to us.

159
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:40,380
I guarantee this kind of thing

160
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,950
will absolutely never happen again, okay?

161
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:01,500
Chuck, the key issue here

162
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:04,380
isn't whether you write a self-reflection or not.

163
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:05,820
It's whether you can control

164
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:08,220
that big mouth of yours that's always craving food.

165
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:10,620
If you can't get a handle on it,

166
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:14,200
writing a 1000 self-reflections won't help. You get that?

167
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:15,900
I get it, Coach.

168
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:18,750
I swear I'll never do it again.

169
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:19,740
I know, I know.

170
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,630
The second I say something, you already "know."

171
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:25,020
You say you know, but I don't
think you know anything at all.

172
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:26,910
We were already

173
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,380
in enough trouble here at Falcon Camp.

174
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:31,740
You- you're just making things harder for me!

175
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:34,140
Coach, what kind of trouble are we in?

176
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:37,500
Nothing major.

177
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:40,860
Stealing things is just so humiliating, isn't it?

178
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:42,300
Coach.

179
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:45,350
Those two cooks said they wanted to kick us out!

180
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:46,510
What do we do?

181
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:50,460
About that... you don't have to worry for now.

182
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:51,910
I just talked to Manager Ma.

183
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:55,740
This time, he's letting it slide.

184
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:01,500
I'm giving everyone a serious warning today.

185
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:04,860
From now on, if any Team member dares to break the rules again,

186
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:08,190
and bring shame to the Jianghai Team,
they will be kicked off the Team immediately.

187
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,110
There will be zero tolerance. Do you all hear me clearly?

188
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,580
We understand.

189
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,980
Chuck, did you hear it clearly?

190
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:16,860
I heard you.

191
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,660
And as for you, Mark.

192
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:24,540
As the Captain, I put you in charge of this Team.

193
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,420
You failed to lead them well,
so you share the responsibility.

194
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:29,340
Coach.

195
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,010
That day, Chuck lied to the Captain and said

196
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:32,700
he had to use the bathroom.

197
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:34,590
I don't want to hear excuses.

198
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,580
He's the Captain.

199
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:37,500
I told him to lead the Team well, and he didn't do it.

200
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,900
He bears undeniable responsibility for this.

201
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:44,220
Mark, you tell me right now.

202
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:46,620
While I was away from the Team,

203
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,540
who else broke the rules?

204
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,660
What's going on here?

205
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:01,500
Coach Tony.

206
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:05,340
Coach Tony.

207
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,260
And you are?

208
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:10,620
I'm Monica's mother, Marilyn.

209
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,980
Oh, Monica's mom! I've heard so much about you.

210
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:17,250
I've been waiting for you for days.

211
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:18,780
Really?

212
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:22,140
I have some thoughts I wanted to share.

213
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,580
Could we talk for a moment?

214
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,420
Oh, talk? Sure, sure.

215
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:31,260
Mark, where are the notes I asked you to give to the Coach?

216
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:46,620
See, if I hadn't come,

217
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:50,940
my suggestions would've just stayed
buried in your pocket forever.

218
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:55,740
Coach, take a look.

219
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:56,700
Okay, okay.

220
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,980
Shall we talk over there?

221
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,390
Okay, okay.

222
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:04,380
After you.

223
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,580
"Regarding the Jianghai Team's Training Camp Life."

224
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:14,460
"A Few Suggestions on Nutritional Balance."

225
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:16,380
Coach Tony.

226
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,750
This is the result of my careful observation

227
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:19,740
of your Training life here.

228
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,620
I've put together 35 specific suggestions.

229
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:26,460
Here, let me walk you through them in detail.

230
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,380
First of all.

231
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:31,620
We must ensure a basic level of
nutritional balance for the kids every day.

232
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:37,500
The first key point is breakfast.

233
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:38,940
For breakfast,

234
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,340
They must have one egg and one piece of bread.

235
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,740
Whole wheat bread is best. And also,

236
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:45,660
there needs to be some fruit.

237
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:48,510
Preferably apples, bananas, tomatoes,

238
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,980
cucumbers, and the like.

239
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:54,300
I suggest that these fruits should be rotated regularly.

240
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:56,190
Oh, right, right!

241
00:14:56,195 --> 00:14:56,199
And most importantly,

242
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:58,620
The absolute most important thing is milk.

243
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:01,020
It must be pure, fresh milk.

244
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:03,150
Because calcium intake is

245
00:15:03,330 --> 00:15:04,880
the most crucial and important thing for adolescents.

246
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:08,220
If the other nutritional components aren't balanced properly,

247
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:11,580
then the calcium won't be absorbed effectively.

248
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:14,940
That leads me to my 2nd point.

249
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Time out!

250
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:20,670
Ms. Marilyn, regarding this feedback of yours,

251
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:23,070
I'll take it and read through it carefully later, okay?

252
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:24,030
Okay, okay.

253
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:24,540
Take your time.

254
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:26,460
Coach Tony, wait!

255
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:28,350
I've also made detailed suggestions

256
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,820
for your daily meals.

257
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:32,220
Now let me explain

258
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:33,660
the weekly nutritional plan to you.

259
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:36,060
It can be roughly summarized as follows:

260
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:38,940
Each week must ensure a variety of meats.

261
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:42,300
All types of organ meats need to be included at least once.

262
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:45,660
If varying the types of meat is too difficult,

263
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:48,060
then I suggest making fish the primary protein source.

264
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,940
But you must guarantee they eat seafood at least once.

265
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:54,780
Therefore, I propose the following:

266
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,220
The 1st point is...

267
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:04,860
Ms. Marilyn, I completely agree with your suggestions.

268
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:08,220
However, this is a Training Camp.

269
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:10,620
We can't meet the kind of standards

270
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:13,500
you'd find at a Nutrition Research Institute.

271
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:15,900
What is that supposed to mean?

272
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:18,800
I entrusted my child to you for Training.

273
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,720
Can't I even demand that my child

274
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:22,620
receive basic nutritional assurance?

275
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:26,910
The purpose of our training Camp

276
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:29,340
is to improve their Yo-Yo skills while simultaneously

277
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:31,260
forging their willpower and character.

278
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:35,100
This Camp is specifically designed to
cultivate a spirit of Perseverance.

279
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:37,940
Of course, the conditions here
can't compare to being at home.

280
00:16:38,620 --> 00:16:40,860
Coach Tony, hearing you say that

281
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:42,780
makes me even more uneasy.

282
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:46,210
You haven't taken my words to heart at all.

283
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,540
Do you think my requests are unreasonable?

284
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,390
These are the absolute minimum conditions

285
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:52,860
for ensuring a child's healthy growth!

286
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:55,260
Please believe me when I say this.

287
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:59,100
Even if the meal standards for this 1 month

288
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:02,940
don't meet the balanced nutrition you're asking for,

289
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:05,820
it won't have any serious negative consequences

290
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:09,180
on the Kids' long-term development.

291
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:11,100
Just listening to you talk, I can tell

292
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:14,940
you don't know the first thing about nutrition.

293
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,340
In this heat,

294
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:19,230
you should at least be providing the kids

295
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:20,700
with some cold refreshments!

296
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:25,010
We do have those! We really do have them!

297
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:27,900
Ms. Marilyn,

298
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:31,710
I will definitely take your suggestions into serious consideration.

299
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:33,660
And to the best of my ability,

300
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:36,540
I'll try to improve the conditions here at Camp.

301
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:38,940
But at the same time, I also have

302
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,340
a small request for you.

303
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:44,220
I hope

304
00:17:45,340 --> 00:17:47,580
that you won't continue staying here
accompanying your Daughter anymore.

305
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,420
That will only cause your Child to develop

306
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:53,820
a sense of dependency.

307
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,220
And then our Training Camp won't achieve its purpose.

308
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:58,620
So, when it comes down to it,

309
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:01,020
you're just trying to get rid of me, right?

310
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:02,000
No!

311
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:05,340
And the more you try to push me away,
the less I trust this place!

312
00:18:05,980 --> 00:18:07,260
Let me tell you.

313
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,150
I will stay.

314
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,620
And I'm staying until the very end.

315
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:23,100
Oh, man.

316
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:34,140
Monica.

317
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:44,700
Can't you go talk to your Mom and
try to get her to see reason?

318
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,000
I...

319
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:48,060
Coach.

320
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,940
If even Monica can't do anything about her Mom, then who can?

321
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:53,340
Who else could possibly do it?

322
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:57,660
You're not suggesting we send the Captain to talk to her, are you?

323
00:18:58,120 --> 00:18:58,620
Don't be ridiculous.

324
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:02,460
I think the best solution

325
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:03,900
is for Monica to just stay with her Mom

326
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:05,340
and not come to Training.

327
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:07,230
That way, her Mom  will stop

328
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:08,900
showing up to disrupt our practice.

329
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:10,620
That's a great idea!

330
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:15,420
What do you mean "great idea"? That's a terrible idea.

331
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:19,710
Monica is our Teammate.

332
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:20,990
How can she just skip Training?

333
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,140
But Coach.

334
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:24,060
If Monica's Mom is hovering around

335
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:25,500
watching us train the whole time,

336
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,900
then there's no way we'll be able to get any real practice done.

337
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:40,860
Looks like you're the only one who can really fix this, Monica.

338
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:15,420
Monica.

339
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:16,740
Did you knock on the wrong door?

340
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:19,260
What do you mean, "wrong door"?

341
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:21,660
Monica, you came to see me, right?

342
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:25,980
I... I wanted to ask you guys for a favor.

343
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:47,870
1, 2, 3, 4!

344
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,660
Ahhhh! Help!

345
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,580
It's that room! It's this one!

346
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:15,900
Oh my god, help! Help me!

347
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:18,300
What's wrong?

348
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:21,180
Under the bed... there's a...

349
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:23,100
There's a what?

